VeridianOS: KSDCMapping: unmap the shared cache segment once, not twice

Real bug, found while fixing the warning in 0001 (not reported by GCC).
KSDCMapping::detachFromSharedMemory() called ::munmap(m_mapped, m_mapSize)
unconditionally and then called it again in the error check:

    ::munmap(m_mapped, m_mapSize);
    if (0 != ::munmap(m_mapped, m_mapSize)) { ...log... }

The second call unmaps an address range the process no longer owns. In a
multi-threaded process another thread can have received a new mapping at
that address in between (mmap reuses freed ranges), and the second munmap()
then silently unmaps that unrelated memory; otherwise it is a no-op and the
error check can never see the first call's failure. Keep only the checked
call. Applies after 0001.

diff -ru a/src/lib/caching/ksdcmapping_p.h b/src/lib/caching/ksdcmapping_p.h
--- a/src/lib/caching/ksdcmapping_p.h	2026-10-08 17:30:32.622028044 -0400
+++ b/src/lib/caching/ksdcmapping_p.h	2026-10-08 17:30:32.649398696 -0400
@@ -162,7 +162,6 @@
                 ::msync(m_mapped, m_mapSize, MS_INVALIDATE | MS_ASYNC);
             }
 #endif
-            ::munmap(m_mapped, m_mapSize);
             if (0 != ::munmap(m_mapped, m_mapSize)) {
                 qCCritical(KCOREADDONS_DEBUG) << "Unable to unmap shared memory segment" << static_cast<void *>(m_mapped) << ":" << ::strerror(errno);
             }
